  </header>

  <main>
    <section class="hero" id="home">
      <div class="container hero-inner">
        <div>
          <p class="section-kicker">Structure. Intelligence. Impact.</p>
          <h1><span class="hero-title-line">We build the <span class="accent">structure</span> that</span><span class="hero-title-line">unlocks potential.</span></h1>
          <p class="hero-copy">Trellis Works starts with how your business actually works. We find where time, effort and resources are being lost, then design practical systems that give your team more capacity to focus on what matters.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button button-brass" href={contactHref} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Let&apos;s Talk</a>
            <a class="button button-ghost" href="#services">Explore Services</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="paper-section" id="system">
      <div class="container two-col">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow-rule"></div>
          <p class="section-kicker">What Trellis Works does</p>
          <h2>We look at the whole system.</h2>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="section-intro">Most operational challenges don’t sit neatly in one place. Trellis Works looks across <strong>people, processes, information, systems and technology</strong> to understand where work is getting stuck, repeated or unnecessarily complicated.</p>
          <p class="section-intro">From there, we identify where change will have the greatest impact and recommend the right solution, whether that means redesigning a workflow, connecting existing tools, introducing automation or AI, or simply creating a clearer way of working.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="paper-section" id="services">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="section-kicker">Services</p>
        <h2>From opportunity to working system.</h2>
        <p class="service-lead">We help organizations identify where AI and automation can create real capacity, then design and build practical solutions around the way the business actually works. Engagements can start with an assessment or carry through from opportunity identification to implementation and adoption.</p>

        <div class="services-list">
          <article class="service-item">
            <div class="service-number">1.0</div>
            <div class="service-main">
              <h3>AI Opportunity &amp; Readiness Assessment</h3>
              <p class="service-tagline">Find where AI can actually help.</p>
              <p>We review your workflows, systems, data and recurring work to identify where AI, automation or existing technology could save time, reduce manual effort or create capacity. Rather than a generic AI strategy, you leave with a prioritized set of opportunities based on value, effort and readiness.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="service-side">
              <p class="service-side-title">Typical outputs</p>
              <ul>
                <li>Process and workflow review</li>
                <li>AI and automation opportunity shortlist</li>
                <li>Readiness and feasibility assessment</li>
                <li>Prioritized roadmap</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="service-item">
            <div class="service-number">2.0</div>
            <div class="service-main">
              <h3>Process &amp; Automation Design</h3>
              <p class="service-tagline">Design the way the work should happen.</p>
              <p>We map how work happens today, identify the repetitive steps, handoffs and manual effort that can be removed, and design a practical future-state workflow around the people and systems already in place. Sometimes the answer is automation. Sometimes it’s AI. Sometimes it’s simply changing the process before adding either.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="service-side">
              <p class="service-side-title">Typical outputs</p>
              <ul>
                <li>Current-state workflow mapping</li>
                <li>Automation and AI candidates</li>
                <li>Future-state workflow design</li>
                <li>Implementation plan</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="service-item">
            <div class="service-number">3.0</div>
            <div class="service-main">
              <h3>Intelligent Systems Build</h3>
              <p class="service-tagline">Turn the opportunity into something your team can actually use.</p>
              <p>Trellis Works designs and builds practical AI-enabled tools, automations and integrations around real business workflows. That might include a system that answers and routes incoming inquiries, searches internal knowledge, assembles recurring reports, moves information between systems, drafts routine communications or supports a team through a multi-step workflow.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="service-side">
              <p class="service-side-title">Examples</p>
              <ul>
                <li>AI assistants and workflow agents</li>
                <li>Knowledge and document retrieval</li>
                <li>Automated reporting</li>
                <li>Email and inquiry workflows</li>
                <li>System integrations</li>
                <li>Custom internal tools</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="service-item">
            <div class="service-number">4.0</div>
            <div class="service-main">
              <h3>Enablement &amp; Governance</h3>
              <p class="service-tagline">Leave the capability with your team.</p>
              <p>We help teams understand, use and manage the systems we put in place. That includes practical training, documentation, usage standards and appropriate guardrails so the solution doesn’t become something only the consultant knows how to operate.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="service-side">
              <p class="service-side-title">Typical support</p>
              <ul>
                <li>Team training</li>
                <li>Process and system documentation</li>
                <li>AI usage standards</li>
                <li>Risk and governance guidance</li>
                <li>Ongoing optimization and advisory</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ink-section" id="approach">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="section-kicker">Approach</p>
        <h2>Structure. Intelligence. Impact.</h2>
        <p class="service-lead" style="color: rgba(246, 244, 238, 0.82); max-width: 860px;">We start with the way the business actually works, build the right solution around it, and measure success by what changes for the people doing the work.</p>

        <div class="approach-wrap">
          <article class="approach-card">
            <div class="approach-number">01</div>
            <h3>Structure</h3>
            <p><strong>Understand the work before changing it.</strong></p>
            <p>We map the process, systems, information and handoffs behind the work to understand where friction exists and where time or effort is being lost.</p>
            <p>The goal is not to redesign everything. It is to identify the parts of the system that are worth changing.</p>
          </article>

          <article class="approach-card">
            <div class="approach-number">02</div>
            <h3>Intelligence</h3>
            <p><strong>Use the right tool for the problem.</strong></p>
            <p>Once the opportunity is clear, we determine what should change and how technology can support it. That may include workflow redesign, automation, AI, system integration or a combination of approaches.</p>
            <p>We do not start with the technology. We start with the problem it needs to solve.</p>
          </article>

          <article class="approach-card">
            <div class="approach-number">03</div>
            <h3>Impact</h3>
            <p><strong>Build for a measurable outcome.</strong></p>
            <p>Every engagement should create something tangible: fewer manual steps, faster access to information, less administrative work, more consistent decisions, or more capacity for the team.</p>
            <p>The value of the solution is measured by what changes in the work.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="paper-section" id="about">
      <div class="container about-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="section-kicker">About</p>
          <h2>Built around the problem, not the tool.</h2>
          <p class="section-intro">Technology is only useful when it solves the right problem.</p>
          <p class="section-intro">Trellis Works starts by understanding how work happens today: the processes, systems, information and constraints that shape it. From there, we identify where change can create meaningful value and determine the right approach, whether that involves process redesign, existing technology, automation, AI or a combination of solutions.</p>
          <p class="section-intro">The objective is not to introduce more tools. It is to create practical systems that reduce friction, support the people doing the work, and improve how the business operates.</p>
        </div>
        <aside class="about-note">
          <h3>What Trellis Works is designed to do</h3>
          <p>Give organizations a practical way to assess where capacity is being lost, where systems are getting in the way, and where AI, automation or better workflow design can create meaningful operational improvements.</p>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ink-section" id="contact">
      <div class="container contact-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="section-kicker">Contact</p>
          <h2>Let’s build together.</h2>
          <p class="section-intro" style="color: rgba(246, 244, 238, 0.86);">If you’re looking at a process, system or workload and thinking there has to be a better way to do this, that’s usually a good place to start.</p>
          <p class="section-intro" style="color: rgba(246, 244, 238, 0.86);">Tell us what’s getting in the way, and we’ll help you figure out what should change.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions" style="margin-top: 30px;">
            <a class="button button-brass" href={contactHref} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Start a conversation</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="contact-card">
          <h3>Contact details</h3>
          <ul class="contact-list" style="margin-top: 18px;">
            <li>
              <span class="contact-label">Email</span>
              <span class="contact-value"><a href={contactHref} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">info@trellisworks.ca</a></span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="contact-label">Location</span>
              <span class="contact-value">1004 8 Ave SE<br/>Calgary, AB T2G 0M4</span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="contact-label">Next step</span>
              <span class="contact-value">Reach out by email to start the conversation.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="site-footer">
    <div class="container footer-inner">
      <div class="footer-brand">Trellis Works</div>
      <div class="footer-links">
        <a href="#services">Services</a>
        <a href="#approach">Approach</a>
        <a href="#about">About</a>
        <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
        <a href={contactHref} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">info@trellisworks.ca</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </footer>

  <script>
    const header = document.querySelector('.site-header');
    const updateHeaderHeight = () => {
      if (header) {
        document.documentElement.style.setProperty('--header-height', `${header.getBoundingClientRect().height}px`);
      }
    };
    updateHeaderHeight();
    if (header && 'ResizeObserver' in window) {
      new ResizeObserver(updateHeaderHeight).observe(header);
    }

    const toggle = document.getElementById('mobileToggle');
    const navWrap = document.getElementById('navWrap');
    const navLinks = navWrap?.querySelectorAll('a') ?? [];

    if (toggle && navWrap) {
      toggle.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const isOpen = navWrap.classList.toggle('open');
        toggle.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(isOpen));
        toggle.setAttribute('aria-label', isOpen ? 'Close menu' : 'Open menu');
      });

      navLinks.forEach(link => {
        link.addEventListener('click', () => {
          navWrap.classList.remove('open');
          toggle.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
          toggle.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Open menu');
        });
      });
    }
  </script>
</Layout>

